MID_SE_Tob_Lys_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_001: Ooo... The stars are pretty tonight— Hic!\nDon't you think so, Sander?
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_002: My name is Lysander, Commander Tobias. The hour\nis already late. We should return to base.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_003: Eh, don't sweat it. You haven't had enough wine yet.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_004: Sorry to say, sir, but I'm not drinking. I don't have\nmuch tolerance for wine.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_005: Boo—hic!—ooo. You're no fun, Sander. Oooh?\nI'm feeling kinda wobbly...
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_006: Again, it's "Lysander." And you've had too much\nto drink.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_007: I'll lend you my shoulder. Just put your arm here...
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_008: Mmph. Hm? What's this glittery...sparkly thing?
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_009: The brooch? It was a gift from the late King Sergio.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_010: Oh yeah? Looks nice. Real pretty.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_011: It was given in honor of my father Kleitos for his\ndeeds during the War of Grania.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_012: After my father died an honorable death, King\nSergio told me, "I owe your father much."
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_013: I only learned later that it's a one-of-a-kind piece\nby one of the king's own artisans.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_014: Ooh... *yawn* Pretty nifty...
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_015: Yes, this brooch is a mark of my father's loyalty and\nthe king's trust in him.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_016: Oh! But Commander Tobias, you also earned\nmilitary renown in the War of Grania.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_017: Would you mind telling me what sort of man my\nfather was from your perspective?
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_018: *snore* Klei was incredible... *snore*
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_019: Commander! You'll catch a cold if you sleep in\nthe middle of the road!
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_020: Ahhh, shut your trap... Oh, I got an idea.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_021: There's a warm-lookin' bed...just...over there...
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_022: Commander, no! That's the bedding for the yarcs!
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_023: So? Hic! I'm sleepin' there, like it or not.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_024: The Lionheart of Saramis cannot be allowed to\nbed down with livestock!
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_025: Don't worry... I'm not gonna let—hic!—a buncha\nyarcs...get the drop on me!
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_C_026: This is one of Saramis's most decorated heroes?\nIf he weren't my superior, I'd pour water on him.
MID_SE_Tob_Lys_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_001: You look upset, Sander. Got a stomachache?
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_002: It's "Lysander." And I'm in peak condition.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_003: It's just that when you asked me to help carry\nluggage, I thought it would be military supplies.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_004: Not your own personal casks of wine.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_005: What, are you jealous? C'mon, get lifting!
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_006: Whew! I owe you one. Go on, take a couple for\nyour trouble.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_007: I'll abstain, thank you. I'm not overly fond of wine.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_008: Boooo. Then again, this is all the cheap stuff.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_009: The pricey stuff tastes better, but you can't drink\nas much of it.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_010: So this works for me! I can drink it like a fish.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_011: {SetColor=Gray}Commander Tobias loves his wine, but I wonder\nif he takes it too far.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_012: {SetColor=Gray}I've never seen him spend money on anything other\nthan wine or mead.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_013: Out of curiosity, how many days will this last you?
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_014: Huh. Not sure. If I'm in the mood, I could probably\nempty these in a night.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_015: One night?! Then your thirst must be practically\nbottomless!
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_016: Wish I could just dive into a lake of wine. Oh well.\nSee you around, Sander!
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_017: Hrm. This is alarming.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_018: Like Father, Commander Tobias did great things\nduring the War of Grania.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_019: I cannot leave the Lionheart of Saramis in such\na state!
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_020: Is he really squandering his wages on these\nfrivolous indulgences?
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_B_021: If so, I must intervene to help him change his ways!
MID_SE_Tob_Lys_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_001: *gulp* Ahhh! Oh, the wine's extra tasty today.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_002: Commander Tobias? Might I take the spot\nbeside you?
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_003: Go right ahead! You want a cask, Sander?
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_004: I...don't think I can drink that much, but I'll take\na glass or two.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_005: Something on your mind? You seem kinda down.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_006: Yes, well. I have to apologize. I believe I've\nmisjudged you.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_007: I know this was overstepping, but I've gone through\nyour finances, Commander.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_008: Oh? What for?
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_009: Well... I was worried you were spending everything\nyou had on cheap ale.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_010: But I was very wrong. For all those honors you\nreceived during the War of Grania...
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_011: you begged the king to send your rewards to the\nbereaved families of our lost soldiers.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_012: Um... Yeah... I guess I did do that.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_013: Even the golden brooch we spoke of—it was a gift\nfrom the king, but I traced it ultimately to you.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_014: Eh, not quite. King Sergio would've given you that\neven if I didn't say anything.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_015: Kleitos was just that great a warrior. The whole\nkingdom mourned his death.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_016: All I really did was pony up some extra dough.\nYou got a fancy brooch out of the deal.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_017: Then I thank you for that. It has been an important\nkeepsake and good-luck charm for me.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_018: I can't be the only grief-stricken child who benefited\nfrom your generosity.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_019: It was nothing. I don't have a wife or kids of my own.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_020: It's enough to be the kinda guy I can be proud of.\nGold would be wasted on me.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_021: Commander Tobias, I ask your forgiveness for my\npast impropriety.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_022: Baw haw haw! "Impropriety"?! What the hell are you\ntalking about, Sander?
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_023: If I had any luck with the ladies, maybe I WOULD\nhave a family of my own.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_024: You though—I hear you got a new sweetheart every\nnight! Sander the Lady-Killer!
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_025: It's "Lysander"! Can you please get it right just once?!
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_026: Hmm, that's a toughie. Maybe if you were stronger,\nit'd stick in my mind better.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_027: Ugh. Then I'll show you.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_028: One day, my name will ring out so far and wide that\neven you'll remember it.
MID_SE_Tov_Lys_A_029: Looking forward to it, son of Kleitos!